  "references": {
    "1": {
      "note": "Normal leaf stages start individually: Worker at build, Reviewer at freeze and Curator after code PASS; required notices reach Manager before direct peer handovers. Messaging resolves one live seat or refuses ambiguity. A message to a recipient already in a turn may be held until that turn ends, and a recipient at a permission prompt is never sent a message, because that would answer the permission. The product's active sweep or ended-turn drain delivers admissible held work without sender resubmission. CODE and MEMORY keep separate recorded counts under the settings limit and recorded extra-round authority. Manager retains gate and transaction ownership and relays no peer contents.",
